      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-08T22:55:40Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): probing hooks for the Tormach PathPilot post (G38.2)\n\nVoice onProbeMove / onProbeRetreat / onProbeResult in tormach.cps in\nLinuxCNC words, from the LinuxCNC G-code reference and Tormach's\nPathPilot post-processor guidelines: each touch is G38.2 (the control\nhalts on no contact), the trip is read from #5061-#5063 (the WCS the G38\nran in), the back-off is incremental (G91 ... G90), a deviation past the\ntolerance shows (MSG, ...) and ends the program (M2) inside a uniquely\nnumbered o-word if/endif, and the work offset is set with G10 L20 from\nthe current position #5420-#5422 minus the deviation (exact in program\nunits, unlike G10 L2 from #5221..). Without an offset to set the program\nstops for the operator (MSG + M0). A section stating 0 rpm (a touch\nprobe) starts no spindle, writes no belt note and turns on no coolant.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/probe_tormach.rs with face / edge / outside\ncorner / bore / boss goldens on the 770MX (inch) and a metric bore under\ngolden/nc/tormach/, and probe_op.rs the_tormach_post_probes_the_op_with_g38_2.\n\nFixes #362\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
