      "message": "fix(post): Tormach probe deviations are bracketed LinuxCNC expressions\n\nPathPilot Hub 2.14.4 refused probe_face.nc at `#190=#102-0.7874` with\n\"Bad character '-' used\": LinuxCNC evaluates arithmetic only inside\nbrackets. Each deviation is now `#n=[mean-expected]`, and the expected\nvalue's sign is folded into the operator, so an edge or corner probe\n(negative expected value) no longer writes `#100--0.0787`.\n\nPinned by assignments_are_bracketed, called from every probe_tormach\ngolden test; the six goldens are regenerated.\n\nRefs #362\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
